<title>UK: Tomkins up as market-makers adjust position.</title>
<headline>Tomkins up as market-makers adjust position.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in conglomerate Tomkins Plc gained 7-1/2 pence to 273-1/2 in technical trading dominated by market-makers.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no real business going on,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>He said market-makers were adjusting their positions before the year-end and that Tomkins had been propped up over the past two weeks when good demand was noted from a limited number of investors.</p>
<p>Tomkins' shares have been on the way up since December 13 when they closed at 245 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
